commit 062ee0c4b7768ea5b16b8bb19b5575363ed053e0

C03: a screen reading composes from the recognized text, not from the layout receipt (SCREEN1409)

SCREEN1407 measured the reviewed screen reading with the read running: capture approved, completed and verified, ocr.read completed and verified without a second confirmation, and no final. The composer sent the whole ocr.read situation in its prompt (about 32 KB of layout boxes, hashes and timestamps), 31.5 K characters against a 4096-token context ceiling, so every attempt failed before the model; reproduced offline with the real receipt.

llm._compose_situation_payload: for ocr.read the payload keeps the recognized text (bounded to 2000 characters, flagged when truncated), the line count and the language; layout, hashes and timestamps stay in the receipt. The prompt for the same receipt is 2.7 K characters.
llm._compose_situation_payload: a verified ocr.read gets the dense output budget (512 tokens) so a transcription is not cut mid-sentence.

No .NET change. Offline probe only; tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


